l behavior of FK-Ising is highlighted, which is completely missing from the case of standard percolation: in any monotone coupling of FK configurations $\\omega_p$ (e.g., in the one introduced in [Gri95]), as one raises $p$ near $p_c$, the new edges arrive in a self-organized way, so that the correlation length is not governed anymore by the number of pivotal edges at criticality.\nL18: Comments:  | 34 pages, 8 figures. This is a streamlined version; the previous one contains more explanations and additional material on exceptional times in FK models with general $q$. Furthermore, the statement and proof of Theorem 1.2 have slightly changed\nL19: Subjects:  | Probability (math.PR); Mathematical Physics (math-ph)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:1111.0144 [math.PR]\nL21:    | (or cite12†arXiv:1111.0144v4 [math.PR] for this version)\nL22:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1111.0144†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: Journal reference:  | Comm. Math. Phys. 326 (2014), no. 1, 1--35\nL24: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | cite14†https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-013-1857-0†doi.org DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Gábor Pete [cite15†view email ]\nL28: cite5†[v1] Tue, 1 Nov 2011 08:41:16 UTC (333 KB)\nL29: cite16†[v2] Wed, 16 Nov 2011 18:32:31 UTC (333 KB)\nL30: cite17†[v3] Sat, 28 Apr 2012 18:11:51 UTC (316 KB)\nL31: [v4] Thu, 13 Feb 2014 22:48:01 UTC (145 KB)\nL32: \nL33: Full-text links:\nL34: \nL35: ## Access Paper:\nL36: \nL37: View a PDF of the paper titled The near-critical planar FK-Ising model, by Hugo Duminil-Copin and Christophe Garban and G\\'abor Pete\nL38: \nL39:   * cite9†View PDF L40:   * cite10†HTML (experimental) L41:   * cite18†TeX Source L42: \nL43: cite19†view license L44: ### Current browse context:\nL45: \nL46: math.PR\nL47: \nL48: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L49: \nL50: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2011-11 L51: \nL52